      "writtenOn": "2018-10-15T21:10:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In ISH, its i2c pins can be configured as ISH-i2c or HOST-GPIO at boot time by coreboot.\nSame for ISH-GPIOs can be configured as HOST-GPIOs at boot time by coreboot as well. \nWith current ISH silicon, ISH-GPIO and ISH-I2c are physically different pins and cannot be configured by ISH itself.",
      "parentUuid": "e92d5702_76d1017b",
      "revId": "3384ce12f332898899d1fb9a21729ee42bb13935",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
